{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1522307679,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE1NDcyMzgzNTE="},"added":["performance"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1522323375,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NzIwNzcxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2354#issuecomment-377207711"},"message":"Is that in v6 since you used git add in the last command?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1522323496,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NzIwODEzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2354#issuecomment-377208133"},"message":"No V5.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1522774262,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3ODMxOTMwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2354#issuecomment-378319300"},"message":"Michael Hanke wrote:\n\u003e When I bypass unlock with a bash for-loop (likely not the fastest approach), I\n\u003e am 4-5x faster -- and seemingly achieve the same result:\n \nUnlock has different code paths for v5 and v6, so it matters which one\nyou're using. Probably v6 is faster; I'll assume you're using v5 for now..\n\nOne significant thing unlock does is it looks to see if the file\nhas been committed to HEAD. This had to be done to avoid a complex\nsituation with the pre-commit hook, as explained in commit\nfd55563b02dd8fedbb2420f440603be7192d94dc. Without that HEAD lookup,\nI benchmark unlock as running approx 300% faster.\n\nSo I think that's the main overhead compared to cp. Unlock also does a\nfew little things like statting the symlink to find the key, etc.\n\nI suppose unlock could check once if the working tree is all committed\nto HEAD, and so avoid the per-file checks. If that can be done\ncheaply enough. (git status --porcelain). There would be a slightly\nwider potential race than the one that already exists around the check.\nIt might make sense to only have --fast enable that, with appropriate\nwarnings in the documentation.\n\n\u003e Moreover: Putting the modified files back into annex is also slow. While that\n\u003e actually requires some more work, it should not be much more than what fsck\n\u003e does, and probably not more than fsck and unlock combined, but that is the case\n\u003e here:\n\u003e \n\u003e % git add .\n\u003e git add .  10.31s user 1.57s system 99% cpu 11.929 total\n\u003e ...\n\u003e git commit --amend  588.24s user 46.04s system 100% cpu 10:28.18 total\n\nThat's kind of the least efficient way to do it, since you're staging\nthe whole file content into the index and then letting the pre-commit\nhook convert that back to annexed symlinks. git annex add would probably\nbe faster.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537365944,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMjgxNzExNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2354#issuecomment-422817117"},"message":"FTR: Re-evaluating the situation with annex 6.20180913+git33-g2cd5a723f-1~ndall+1 and a different dataset (5.4k files @ 21kb each)\n\n\u003e unlock in v5\ngit annex unlock .  24.07s user 3.87s system 103% cpu 27.027 total\n\u003e for reference\ngit annex fsck  14.24s user 1.66s system 108% cpu 14.704 total\n\u003e straight cp\n% time bash -c 'for i in $(find . -type l); do cp --remove-destination $(readlink -f $i) $i; done' \nbash -c   9.91s user 3.27s system 104% cpu 12.569 total\n\nFactor 2x for unlock vs. fsck/cp. I assume git annex has been optimized in areas that affect this functionality. Thanks!\n\nClosing...","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537365944,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTg1NTE1MzQ0NQ=="},"status":2}]}